        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 29, 2025</p>

        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Sign-Speak-AI, our South African Sign Language (SASL) detection web application ("the Application," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and protects information in connection with this university research project.</p>
        <p>We are committed to protecting your privacy and being transparent about our data practices. By using this Application, you consent to the practices described in this Privacy Policy.</p>

        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <h3>2.1 Camera Data</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Real-time Video Input:</strong> The Application accesses your device camera to capture real-time video for sign language detection</li>
          <li><strong>Processing:</strong> Video frames are processed locally in your browser to detect hand gestures and SASL signs</li>
          <li><strong>Storage:</strong> Video data is NOT stored permanently. Video frames are processed in real-time and discarded immediately after processing</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>2.2 Technical Information</h3>
        <p>We may automatically collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser type and version</li>
          <li>Operating system</li>
          <li>Device type (desktop, mobile, tablet)</li>
          <li>Screen resolution</li>
          <li>Time and date of access</li>
          <li>Pages or features accessed within the Application</li>
          <li>Performance metrics (processing time, detection accuracy rates)</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>2.3 Usage Data</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Sign detection results (text output)</li>
          <li>Interaction patterns with the Application</li>
          <li>Error logs and diagnostic information</li>
          <li>Session duration and frequency of use</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>2.4 Voluntary Information</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Feedback or comments you choose to provide</li>
          <li>Survey responses if you participate in research studies</li>
          <li>Demographic information (only if voluntarily provided for research purposes)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
        <h3>3.1 Primary Purposes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Functionality:</strong> To provide sign language detection and text-to-speech conversion services</li>
          <li><strong>Improvement:</strong> To analyze and improve detection accuracy and application performance</li>
          <li><strong>Research:</strong> To conduct academic research on sign language recognition technology</li>
          <li><strong>Development:</strong> To identify bugs, errors, and areas for technical enhancement</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>3.2 Academic Research</h3>
        <p>As a university project, collected data may be used for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Academic publications and presentations</li>
          <li>Development of improved sign language detection algorithms</li>
          <li>Statistical analysis of application usage patterns</li>
          <li>Educational purposes within the university</li>
          <li>Thesis or dissertation research</li>
        </ul>
        <p>All research use will involve anonymized and aggregated data unless explicit consent is obtained for other uses.</p>

        <h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>
        <h3>4.1 Local Processing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Video processing occurs locally in your browser</li>
          <li>Camera feeds are NOT transmitted to external servers during normal operation</li>
          <li>No video recordings are saved unless you explicitly grant permission</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>4.2 Data Retention</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Session Data:</strong> Cleared when you close the browser or end your session</li>
          <li><strong>Usage Statistics:</strong> May be retained in anonymized form for research purposes</li>
          <li><strong>Technical Logs:</strong> Retained only as long as necessary for debugging and improvement purposes</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>4.3 Security Measures</h3>
        <p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Secure browser connections (HTTPS where available)</li>
          <li>No permanent storage of sensitive camera data</li>
          <li>Limited data collection practices</li>
          <li>Access controls for any stored data</li>
        </ul>
        <p>However, as this is an educational project, we cannot guarantee absolute security. Use the Application at your own risk.</p>

        <h2>5. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
        <h3>5.1 No Commercial Sharing</h3>
        <p>We do NOT sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties for commercial purposes.</p>
        <h3>5.2 Academic Sharing</h3>
        <p>We may share anonymized, aggregated data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>In academic publications and conference presentations</li>
          <li>With research collaborators within the university</li>
          <li>With the academic community for educational purposes</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>5.3 Legal Requirements</h3>
        <p>We may disclose information if required by:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Law, regulation, or legal process</li>
          <li>Court order or government request</li>
          <li>Protection of rights, safety, or property</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>5.4 Third-Party Services</h3>
        <p>The Application may use third-party libraries or services (e.g., machine learning frameworks, text-to-speech APIs). These services may have their own privacy policies. We are not responsible for third-party privacy practices.</p>

        <h2>6. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
        <h3>6.1 Camera Access Control</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You can deny or revoke camera access at any time through your browser settings</li>
          <li>Denying camera access will prevent the Application from functioning</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>6.2 Browser Controls</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Clear cookies and local storage through your browser settings</li>
          <li>Use private/incognito browsing mode</li>
          <li>Disable JavaScript (though this will prevent the Application from working)</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>6.3 Data Deletion</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Since most data is processed locally and not stored permanently, closing your browser session deletes most information</li>
          <li>For any stored usage statistics, you may request deletion by contacting us</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>6.4 Opt-Out</h3>
        <p>You may opt out of using the Application at any time by simply closing it and not returning.</p>

        <h2>7. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
        <p>The Application may use:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Session Storage:</strong> Temporary storage for application functionality during your session</li>
          <li><strong>Local Storage:</strong> May store user preferences or settings</li>
          <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> May be used for session management or analytics </li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can control cookies and storage through your browser settings.</p>

        <h2>8. International Users</h2>
        <p>This Application is operated from South Africa. If you access the Application from outside South Africa, your information may be transferred to and processed in South Africa. By using the Application, you consent to such transfer and processing.</p>

        <h2>9. Limitations and Disclaimers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We provide no guarantees about data security or privacy</li>
          <li>The Application is provided "as is" without warranties</li>
          <li>We cannot be held liable for unauthorized access or data breaches</li>
          <li>This is NOT a commercial-grade application with enterprise-level security</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be effective immediately upon posting. We will update the "Last Updated" date at the top of this policy. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

        <h2>11. University Context</h2>
        <p>This Application is developed as part of a university project. The university may have additional policies governing research data and student projects. This Privacy Policy operates within that broader framework.</p>

        <h2>12. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>The Application may contain links to external websites or resources. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of third-party sites. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any third-party sites you visit.</p>

        <h2>13. Data Protection Rights</h2>
        <p>Under South African law, including the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA), you may have certain rights regarding your personal information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Right to access your personal information</li>
          <li>Right to correct inaccurate information</li>
          <li>Right to delete your information (subject to legal obligations)</li>
          <li>Right to object to processing</li>
          <li>Right to lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To exercise these rights, please contact us through the university department.</p>

        <h2>14. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>For questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your data, please contact the project team through the university department or supervising faculty member.</p>

        <h2>15. Consent</h2>
        <p>By using this Application, you consent to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The collection and use of information as described in this Privacy Policy</li>
          <li>Camera access for sign language detection</li>
          <li>Use of your anonymized data for academic research purposes</li>
          <li>The limitations and terms outlined in this policy</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>16. Supervisory Authority</h2>
        <p>If you have concerns about how your data is handled, you may contact:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The university's research ethics committee</li>
          <li>The Information Regulator of South Africa (for POPIA-related concerns)</li>
        </ul>

        <hr>
        <p><strong>Academic Project Notice:</strong> This is a university educational project. While we strive to protect your privacy, this Application does not have the same resources or security infrastructure as commercial applications. Use with appropriate caution and understanding of its educational nature.</p>
      </div>
